><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU YASUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAMURA NOBUSHIGE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TERAI HIROMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO YASUMICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, TATSUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU, YASUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAMURA, NOBUSHIGE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TERAI, HIROMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, YASUMICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An artificial blood vessel having the following characteristics: 1) having an antithrombotic effect; 2) having a tissue affinity; 3) being rapidly converted into endothelium; and 4) allowing regeneration of host tissues; and a process for producing the same. The artificial blood vessel is one collected from a heterologous organism from which the cellular constituents of the blood vessel have been completely eliminated. The above process aims at producing this artificial blood vessel and involves the step of washing a blood vessel collected from a heterologous organism with a surfactant to thereby completely eliminate the cellular constituents of the blood vessel therefrom.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un vaisseau sanguin artificiel possédant les propriétés suivantes: (1) un effet antithrombotique; (2) une affinité avec les tissus; (3) une capacité de conversion rapide en endothélium; et (4) la régénération des tissus hôtes. L'invention concerne également un procédé de production de ce vaisseau. Le vaisseau sanguin artificiel est prélevé sur un organisme hétérologue dont on a complètement éliminé les constituants cellulaires du vaisseau sanguin. Le procédé selon l'invention est destiné à la production de ce vaisseau sanguin artificiel et consiste à laver un vaisseau sanguin prélevé sur un organisme hétérologue avec un tensioactif pour en éliminer complètement les constituants cellulaires du vaisseau sanguin.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>